---
// Literal recreation of the Claude Design canvas's Admin Product Info
// screen (project/AdminProductDetail.dc.html -> NavSidebar role="admin"
// + the plain shared NavTop.astro (section="Inventory" parent="Products")
// + PageProductDetail, an admin-only, role-agnostic component — unlike
// PageOrders/PageOrderDetail/PageNewOrder, PageProductDetail.dc.html has
// no role prop at all; AdminProductDetail.dc.html is its only real
// consumer). NOTE: at the start of this turn, no Product Info artboard
// existed anywhere in the design export (checked the full file listing
// and canvas.json) — the user confirmed the canvas had since been
// updated, and AdminProductDetail.dc.html/AdminProductDetailDark.dc.html/
// PageProductDetail.dc.html were re-fetched live from the artifact before
// writing anything here. This is a genuine Admin-shell route
// (/admin/products/[id]) — not linked from/to Sales Products & Stock,
// Inventory Staff Product Lookup, or the old AppShell product-detail form.
//
// SCHEMA REALITY vs THE DESIGN — this is the central finding of this
// screen: PageProductDetail.dc.html assumes a warehouse-management data
// model this schema does not have — per-bin stock locations, reserved/
// available-to-promise quantities, a purchase-order/restock-scheduling
// system (fake "RS-3044" reference + ETA), and a catalog data model with
// brand/HSN/GST/barcode/physical-dimension fields. None of that exists:
// `inventory` is one row per product (quantity_on_hand/reorder_level
// only, no location), `products` has no brand/HSN/GST/barcode/dimension
// columns, and there is no restock-request/PO table anywhere. Every one
// of those is omitted below, never invented. Two things turned out to be
// MORE real than the design's own mockup data, though: `suppliers` has
// real contact_name/phone columns (the design's own supplier contact line
// is therefore reproducible for real, not fabricated, once correctly
// derived), and `inventory_movements` has no stored running-balance
// column but one is exactly reconstructible from real data — see BALANCE
// RECONSTRUCTION below.
//
// Real vs deferred/fabricated, per your explicit no-fabrication rules:
//  - Header: real product name/SKU, real stock-status pill (full 5-value
//    real derivation already used everywhere else), real category pill
//    (or "Uncategorised"), real "{qty} on hand" subtitle (the design's own
//    subtitle mixes a fabricated supplier name into this line and adds a
//    complete fabrication — "40 units arriving 3 Oct on restock RS-3044"
//    — no restock-request/PO system or ETA field exists anywhere; both
//    dropped, kept only the real on-hand count).
//  - "Edit" button: real product-editing capability DOES exist
//    (updateProduct Action, products_update_staff RLS — admin is already
//    authorized) — but no Claude-Design-shell edit form exists anywhere
//    in this project (the old /inventory/products/[id].astro form is
//    old-shell, explicitly not reusable here, same as Admin Products'
//    own "New product" gap last turn). Per your instruction ("if editing
//    is not currently implemented [i.e. no real UI for it exists yet],
//    use an honest unavailable/deferred treatment"), rendered as a real,
//    visibly-present but honestly disabled button ("Not available yet"),
//    not omitted outright — the design shows it unconditionally, and a
//    real backend action for it already exists, unlike "Request restock"
//    below.
//  - "Request restock" button: omitted entirely, not just disabled — no
//    restock-REQUEST workflow exists at all (real restock recording is
//    `record_inventory_movement()`, a direct staff/admin action, not a
//    request-and-fulfill flow), and no Admin-shell screen to land on even
//    exists (no "Admin Receiving" screen anywhere in this project's
//    13-screen list) — there is no honest destination to defer to.
//  - Delete/Request deletion: reused verbatim from Admin Products (same
//    real `deleteProduct` Action for super_admin, same real
//    `requestApproval({actionType:'delete_product'})` for admin) — the
//    exact same permission boundary, not broadened. Placed in the header
//    actions row, matching Admin Order Detail's own convention of real
//    destructive/request actions living in the page header.
//  - Image: real `products.image_url` — shown when present, the design's
//    own honest "No image" placeholder reused verbatim when absent.
//  - "Details" card (Brand/HSN code/GST/Unit/Barcode/Dimensions): none of
//    these columns exist anywhere in the schema — the whole card is
//    replaced with a real equivalent using columns that DO exist and are
//    not shown anywhere else on this screen: `products.description`
//    (or an honest "No description on file"), and real Added/Updated
//    dates (`created_at`/`updated_at`).
//  - "Pricing" card: real Cost (or "—" when null — never computing a
//    margin from a fabricated substitute), real Price, real Margin (both
//    the % and the real ₹ absolute value, only when cost is present).
//    "excl. GST" subtitle dropped (no GST field/rate anywhere).
//  - "Supplier" card: real, not fabricated — same "most recent restock
//    supplier" derivation already proven on Admin Products, now also
//    showing the supplier's real contact_name/phone (real suppliers
//    columns) instead of the design's example contact. "Delivery time"
//    row dropped (no lead-time field on suppliers); "Last restock" kept,
//    real (the derived movement's own created_at). Honest "No restock
//    history for this product" empty state when no restock movement with
//    a supplier exists yet (true for all 5 real products in the live
//    database today — zero real 'restock' movements exist at all).
//  - "Stock by location" card: replaced with a real, single-location
//    "Stock" card (this schema has one inventory row per product, not
//    per-bin) — real On hand, real Low stock level (reorder_level), real
//    status pill. No Bin/Reserved/Available columns (no location or
//    reservation concept exists) and no embedded fabricated restock
//    banner.
//  - "Stock level – last 90 days" chart: genuinely real and derivable —
//    see BALANCE RECONSTRUCTION below — rebuilt as a bespoke inline SVG
//    (same reasoning as Admin Dashboard's revenue chart: ChartCanvas.astro
//    uses the old DESIGN.md token system, which would visually clash with
//    this screen's --sd-* tokens). Honest "No stock movement recorded"
//    empty state when a product has zero movements ever (true for the
//    real CLO-TS-001 product today).
//  - "Movements" table: real Date/Type (full real 5-value movement_type
//    enum: restock/sale/adjustment/damaged/return, not just the design's
//    4 example labels)/Reference/Qty/Balance. "Bin" column dropped (no
//    location data). "Reference" is real and type-dependent: a real order
//    id (linking to the already-approved /admin/orders/[id]) for
//    sale/return movements — the real `reference_order_id` column — a
//    real supplier name for restock, or the real free-text `reason` for
//    adjustment/damaged, "—" otherwise. "Balance" is a real reconstructed
//    running total (see below), not fabricated. "View all" button
//    omitted — every real movement for this product is already shown,
//    same "real count instead of fake pagination" precedent used
//    everywhere else in this project.
//
// BALANCE RECONSTRUCTION: `inventory_movements` has no stored running-
// balance column, and this product's very first real quantity was seeded
// directly into `inventory.quantity_on_hand` at Phase 5, not inserted via
// a movement row — so summing every real quantity_delta for a product
// does NOT equal its current quantity_on_hand (verified live via SQL: the
// two numbers differ by exactly the product's original seeded quantity
// for every one of the 5 real products). The real, exact starting balance
// is solved for arithmetically: quantity_on_hand − sum(all real
// quantity_delta ever) — by definition, walking forward from that number
// through every real movement in chronological order always lands back
// on the real current quantity_on_hand. Both the Movements table's
// "Balance" column and the chart's y-values are this same real,
// internally-consistent reconstruction — never a fabricated number.
import BaseLayout from "../../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import NavSidebar from "../../../components/staff/NavSidebar.astro";
import NavTop from "../../../components/staff/NavTop.astro";
import type { UserRole } from "../../../lib/types";

const { id } = Astro.params;
const viewerRoleRaw = Astro.locals.role as UserRole | null;
const viewerRole = (viewerRoleRaw === "super_admin" ? "super_admin" : "admin") as "admin" | "super_admin";

const { data: product } = await Astro.locals.supabase
  .from("products")
  .select("id, sku, name, description, category_id, categories(name), price, cost, image_url, is_active, created_at, updated_at")
  .eq("id", id)
  .maybeSingle();

if (!product) {
  Astro.response.status = 404;
}

const { data: inv } = product
  ? await Astro.locals.supabase.from("inventory").select("quantity_on_hand, reorder_level").eq("product_id", id).maybeSingle()
  : { data: null };

const { data: movementRows } = product
  ? await Astro.locals.supabase
      .from("inventory_movements")
      .select("id, movement_type, quantity_delta, reason, supplier_id, reference_order_id, performed_by, created_at, suppliers(name, contact_name, phone)")
      .eq("product_id", id)
      .order("created_at", { ascending: true })
  : { data: null };

function categoryOf(row: { categories: unknown } | null): { name: string } | null {
  return (row?.categories as unknown as { name: string } | null) ?? null;
}
function supplierOf(row: { suppliers: unknown }): { name: string; contact_name: string | null; phone: string | null } | null {
  return row.suppliers as unknown as { name: string; contact_name: string | null; phone: string | null } | null;
}

const qty = inv?.quantity_on_hand ?? 0;
const reorderLevel = inv?.reorder_level ?? 0;
const stockTone: "in" | "low" | "out" = qty === 0 ? "out" : qty <= reorderLevel ? "low" : "in";
const STOCK_LABEL: Record<string, string> = { in: "In stock", low: "Low stock", out: "Out of stock" };

const cost = product?.cost === null || product?.cost === undefined ? null : Number(product.cost);
const price = product ? Number(product.price) : 0;
const marginPct = cost !== null && price > 0 ? Math.round(((price - cost) / price) * 100) : null;
const marginAbs = cost !== null ? price - cost : null;

const movements = movementRows ?? [];

// --- Real running-balance reconstruction (see BALANCE RECONSTRUCTION above) ---
const sumOfDeltas = movements.reduce((sum, m) => sum + m.quantity_delta, 0);
const startingBalance = qty - sumOfDeltas;
let running = startingBalance;
const withBalance = movements.map((m) => {
  running += m.quantity_delta;
  return { ...m, balanceAfter: running };
});

// --- Real most-recent-restock supplier (identical derivation to Admin Products) ---
const lastRestock = [...withBalance].reverse().find((m) => m.movement_type === "restock" && m.supplier_id);
const restockSupplier = lastRestock ? supplierOf(lastRestock) : null;

// --- Real Movements table rows (most recent first) ---
const formatCurrency = (value: number) =>
  new Intl.NumberFormat("en-IN", { style: "currency", currency: "INR", maximumFractionDigits: 2 }).format(value);
const formatDate = (value: string) => new Date(value).toLocaleDateString(undefined, { day: "numeric", month: "short" });
const formatDateLong = (value: string) => new Date(value).toLocaleDateString(undefined, { day: "numeric", month: "short", year: "numeric" });

const MOVE_LABEL: Record<string, string> = { restock: "Received", sale: "Sold", adjustment: "Adjusted", damaged: "Damaged", return: "Returned" };
const MOVE_TONE: Record<string, "success" | "outline" | "info" | "danger" | "warn"> = {
  restock: "success",
  sale: "outline",
  adjustment: "info",
  damaged: "danger",
  return: "warn",
};

const movementRowsDisplay = [...withBalance].reverse().map((m) => {
  let refLabel = "—";
  let refHref: string | null = null;
  if ((m.movement_type === "sale" || m.movement_type === "return") && m.reference_order_id) {
    refLabel = m.reference_order_id.slice(0, 8);
    refHref = `/admin/orders/${m.reference_order_id}`;
  } else if (m.movement_type === "restock") {
    refLabel = supplierOf(m)?.name ?? "—";
  } else if (m.reason) {
    refLabel = m.reason;
  }
  return {
    id: m.id,
    date: formatDate(m.created_at),
    type: MOVE_LABEL[m.movement_type] ?? m.movement_type,
    tone: MOVE_TONE[m.movement_type] ?? "outline",
    refLabel,
    refHref,
    qty: m.quantity_delta,
    balance: m.balanceAfter,
  };
});

// --- Real "Stock level" chart (90-day window) ---
const NINETY_DAYS_MS = 90 * 24 * 60 * 60 * 1000;
const windowStart = Date.now() - NINETY_DAYS_MS;
const balanceAtWindowStart = (() => {
  let bal = startingBalance;
  for (const m of withBalance) {
    if (new Date(m.created_at).getTime() >= windowStart) break;
    bal = m.balanceAfter;
  }
  return bal;
})();
const chartMovements = withBalance.filter((m) => new Date(m.created_at).getTime() >= windowStart);
const hasChartData = movements.length > 0;

const CHART_W = 700;
const CHART_H = 160;
const CHART_X_MARGIN = 36;
const CHART_X_RIGHT_PAD = 20;
const chartSeries: { t: number; balance: number }[] = [
  { t: Math.max(windowStart, movements.length > 0 ? new Date(movements[0].created_at).getTime() - NINETY_DAYS_MS : windowStart), balance: balanceAtWindowStart },
  ...chartMovements.map((m) => ({ t: new Date(m.created_at).getTime(), balance: m.balanceAfter })),
  { t: Date.now(), balance: qty },
];
const chartMaxBalance = Math.max(...chartSeries.map((p) => p.balance), reorderLevel, 1);
const chartMinT = windowStart;
const chartMaxT = Date.now();
const chartXOf = (t: number) => CHART_X_MARGIN + ((Math.max(t, chartMinT) - chartMinT) / (chartMaxT - chartMinT || 1)) * CHART_W;
const chartYOf = (bal: number) => CHART_H - (bal / chartMaxBalance) * (CHART_H - 10);
const chartLinePoints = chartSeries.map((p) => `${chartXOf(p.t).toFixed(1)},${chartYOf(p.balance).toFixed(1)}`).join(" ");
const chartAreaPath = `M${chartXOf(chartSeries[0].t).toFixed(1)},${CHART_H} L${chartLinePoints.split(" ").join(" L")} L${chartXOf(chartSeries[chartSeries.length - 1].t).toFixed(1)},${CHART_H} Z`;
const chartReorderY = chartYOf(reorderLevel);
const chartViewboxW = CHART_W + CHART_X_MARGIN + CHART_X_RIGHT_PAD;
---

<BaseLayout title={product ? `${product.name} — Admin` : "Product not found — Admin"}>
  <Fragment slot="head">
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Geist:wght@400;500;600;700&display=swap" />
  </Fragment>

  <div class="sd" id="sd-root">
    <div id="sd-sidebar-backdrop" class="sd__backdrop"></div>

    <div id="sd-sidebar" class="sd__sidebar">
      <NavSidebar active="Products" role="admin" viewerRole={viewerRole} />
    </div>

    <div class="sd__panel">
      <NavTop section="Inventory" parent="Products" page={product ? product.name : "Not found"} />

      <main id="main-content" class="pi__main">
        {
          product ? (
            <Fragment>
              <div class="pi__topbar">
                <a href="/admin/products" class="pi__back">
                  <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="m15 18-6-6 6-6"></path></svg>
                  Products
                </a>
                <div class="pi__header">
                  <div class="pi__heading-col">
                    <div class="pi__heading-row">
                      <h1>{product.name} <span class="pi__sku">· {product.sku}</span></h1>
                      <span class={`pi__pill pi__pill--${stockTone}`}>{STOCK_LABEL[stockTone]}</span>
                      <span class="pi__pill pi__pill--muted">{categoryOf(product)?.name ?? "Uncategorised"}</span>
                      {!product.is_active && <span class="pi__pill pi__pill--muted">Inactive</span>}
                    </div>
                    <span class="pi__meta">{qty} on hand</span>
                  </div>
                  <div class="pi__actions">
                    <button type="button" class="pi__btn" disabled title="Not available yet">
                      <svg width="15" height="15" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M4 20h4L19 9l-4-4L4 16zM13.5 6.5l4 4" /></svg>
                      Edit
                    </button>
                    {viewerRole === "super_admin" ? (
                      <button type="button" class="pi__btn pi__btn--danger" data-action="delete-direct" data-product-id={product.id} data-product-name={product.name}>
                        Delete
                      </button>
                    ) : (
                      <button type="button" class="pi__btn pi__btn--danger" data-action="delete-request" data-product-id={product.id} data-product-name={product.name}>
                        Request deletion
                      </button>
                    )}
                  </div>
                </div>
                <p id="pi-action-message" class="pi__status-message" role="status" />
              </div>

              <div class="pi__body">
                <div class="pi__left">
                  {product.image_url ? (
                    <img src={product.image_url} alt={product.name} class="pi__image" />
                  ) : (
                    <div role="img" aria-label="No product image uploaded" class="pi__image-placeholder">
                      <svg width="32" height="32" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M3 7.5 12 3l9 4.5v9L12 21l-9-4.5zM3 7.5 12 12l9-4.5M12 12v9" /></svg>
                      <span>No image</span>
                    </div>
                  )}

                  <section class="pi__card">
                    <span class="pi__card-title">Product</span>
                    <p class="pi__description">{product.description || "No description on file."}</p>
                    <div class="pi__kv-row"><span class="pi__kv-label">Added</span><span class="pi__kv-value">{formatDateLong(product.created_at)}</span></div>
                    <div class="pi__kv-row"><span class="pi__kv-label">Updated</span><span class="pi__kv-value">{formatDateLong(product.updated_at)}</span></div>
                  </section>

                  <section class="pi__card">
                    <span class="pi__card-title">Pricing</span>
                    <div class="pi__kv-row"><span class="pi__kv-label">Cost</span><span class="pi__kv-value">{cost !== null ? formatCurrency(cost) : "—"}</span></div>
                    <div class="pi__kv-row"><span class="pi__kv-label">Price</span><span class="pi__kv-value">{formatCurrency(price)}</span></div>
                    <div class="pi__divider" />
                    <div class="pi__kv-row">
                      <span class="pi__kv-label">Margin</span>
                      <span class="pi__margin-value">
                        {marginPct !== null ? (
                          <Fragment><span class="pi__margin-pct">{marginPct}%</span> <span class="pi__kv-label">· {formatCurrency(marginAbs!)}</span></Fragment>
                        ) : (
                          "—"
                        )}
                      </span>
                    </div>
                  </section>

                  <section class="pi__card">
                    <span class="pi__card-title">Supplier</span>
                    {restockSupplier ? (
                      <Fragment>
                        <div class="pi__supplier-head">
                          <span class="pi__avatar">
                            {restockSupplier.name.split(" ").filter(Boolean).slice(0, 2).map((p) => p[0]!.toUpperCase()).join("")}
                          </span>
                          <div class="pi__supplier-identity">
                            <span class="pi__supplier-name">{restockSupplier.name}</span>
                            <span class="pi__supplier-contact">{restockSupplier.contact_name ?? "—"}{restockSupplier.phone ? ` · ${restockSupplier.phone}` : ""}</span>
                          </div>
                        </div>
                        <div class="pi__kv-row"><span class="pi__kv-label">Last restock</span><span class="pi__kv-value">{formatDateLong(lastRestock!.created_at)}</span></div>
                      </Fragment>
                    ) : (
                      <p class="pi__empty-note">No restock history for this product.</p>
                    )}
                  </section>
                </div>

                <div class="pi__right">
                  <div class="pi__right-grid">
                    <section class="pi__card">
                      <span class="pi__card-title">Stock</span>
                      <div class="pi__kv-row"><span class="pi__kv-label">On hand</span><span class="pi__kv-value pi__kv-value--big">{qty}</span></div>
                      <div class="pi__kv-row"><span class="pi__kv-label">Low stock level</span><span class="pi__kv-value">{reorderLevel}</span></div>
                      <div class="pi__kv-row"><span class="pi__kv-label">Status</span><span class={`pi__pill pi__pill--${stockTone}`}>{STOCK_LABEL[stockTone]}</span></div>
                    </section>

                    <section class="pi__card">
                      <div class="pi__chart-head">
                        <span class="pi__card-title">Stock level · last 90 days</span>
                        <span class="pi__chart-sub">Units on hand</span>
                      </div>
                      {hasChartData ? (
                        <Fragment>
                          <div class="pi__chart-legend">
                            <span class="pi__legend-item"><span class="pi__legend-swatch pi__legend-swatch--line" /> On hand</span>
                            <span class="pi__legend-item"><span class="pi__legend-swatch pi__legend-swatch--dash" /> Low stock level ({reorderLevel})</span>
                          </div>
                          <svg width="100%" viewBox={`0 0 ${chartViewboxW} ${CHART_H + 24}`} role="img" aria-label={`Stock of ${product.name} over the last 90 days, currently ${qty} on hand`} class="pi__chart-svg">
                            <path d={chartAreaPath} class="pi__chart-area" />
                            <line x1={CHART_X_MARGIN} y1={chartReorderY} x2={CHART_X_MARGIN + CHART_W} y2={chartReorderY} class="pi__chart-reorder-line" />
                            <polyline points={chartLinePoints} class="pi__chart-line" />
                            <circle cx={chartXOf(chartSeries[chartSeries.length - 1].t)} cy={chartYOf(qty)} r="3.5" class="pi__chart-dot" />
                          </svg>
                        </Fragment>
                      ) : (
                        <p class="pi__empty-note">No stock movement recorded for this product.</p>
                      )}
                    </section>
                  </div>

                  <section class="pi__panel-card">
                    <div class="pi__panel-head">
                      <span class="pi__card-title">Movements</span>
                      <span class="pi__panel-sub">{movementRowsDisplay.length} movement{movementRowsDisplay.length === 1 ? "" : "s"}</span>
                    </div>
                    {movementRowsDisplay.length > 0 ? (
                      <Fragment>
                        <div class="pi__grid pi__grid-head">
                          <span>Date</span><span>Type</span><span>Reference</span><span class="pi__col-right">Qty</span><span class="pi__col-right">Balance</span>
                        </div>
                        {movementRowsDisplay.map((m) => (
                          <div class="pi__grid pi__row">
                            <span class="pi__muted-cell">{m.date}</span>
                            <span><span class={`pi__pill pi__pill--${m.tone}`}>{m.type}</span></span>
                            {m.refHref ? (
                              <a href={m.refHref} class="pi__ref-link">{m.refLabel}</a>
                            ) : (
                              <span class="pi__muted-cell pi__ellipsis">{m.refLabel}</span>
                            )}
                            <span class={`pi__col-right pi__qty ${m.qty >= 0 ? "pi__qty--pos" : "pi__qty--neg"}`}>{m.qty >= 0 ? `+${m.qty}` : m.qty}</span>
                            <span class="pi__col-right pi__balance">{m.balance}</span>
                          </div>
                        ))}
                      </Fragment>
                    ) : (
                      <p class="pi__empty-note">No movements recorded for this product.</p>
                    )}
                  </section>
                </div>
              </div>
            </Fragment>
          ) : (
            <div class="pi__notfound">
              <p class="pi__notfound-title">Product not found</p>
              <p class="pi__notfound-body">This product may not exist.</p>
              <a href="/admin/products" class="pi__btn">Back to Products</a>
            </div>
          )
        }
      </main>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .sd {
    --sd-shell: #fafafa;
    --sd-panel: #ffffff;
    --sd-card: #ffffff;
    --sd-fg: #0a0a0a;
    --sd-fg2: #404040;
    --sd-muted: #f5f5f5;
    --sd-muted-fg: #737373;
    --sd-border: #e5e5e5;
    --sd-input: #e5e5e5;
    --sd-primary: #171717;
    --sd-primary-fg: #fafafa;
    --sd-success-bg: #ecfdf3;
    --sd-success-fg: #15803d;
    --sd-warn-bg: #fef3e2;
    --sd-warn-fg: #9a3412;
    --sd-danger-bg: #feecec;
    --sd-danger-fg: #b91c1c;
    --sd-info-bg: #eef2ff;
    --sd-info-fg: #3538cd;
    --sd-accent: #2b50e0;
    --sd-accent-soft: rgba(43, 80, 224, 0.1);
    --sd-chart2: #d9731f;
    --sd-shadow: 0 1px 2px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.05);
    color-scheme: light;

    min-height: 100vh;
    display: flex;
    background: var(--sd-shell);
    color: var(--sd-fg);
    font-family: "Geist", system-ui, sans-serif;
